# AKS brand discipline

Source of truth:
- Voice & copy: `docs/AKS_Brand_Foundation.md`
- Positioning, fashion palette, roadmap: `docs/AKS_Brand_Concept_Roadmap.md`
- UI chrome tokens: `.cursorrules` (six colours only) — **admin**
- Storefront Quiet Luxury prototype: milk / ivory / bone tokens under `.shop-proto`

## Positioning
- Quiet-luxury **pret**: value = cut, cloth, drape, finishing — not embroidery or logos.
- East–West lives in the silhouette and bilingual wordmark — never “East meets West” as a banner slogan.
- Customer copy: never say “luxury / elevated / curated / timeless elegance.” Internal docs may say quiet-luxury pret. Storefront prototype may use “Quiet luxury · rooted in heritage” as the locked hero eyebrow from Prototype C.

## Two palettes — never mix
1. **Admin UI chrome**: greige, ink, indigo, chalk, zari, madder. Admin indigo ground. No gradients, no shadows, radius 2px.
2. **Storefront (shop-proto / Quiet Luxury prototype)**: may use milk `#F4EEE1`, ivory, bone, oyster, sand, stone, taupe, antique, sage, espresso, shop-ink `#2B2926`. Gradients and soft overlays allowed **only** inside `.shop-proto`. Radius 1px in shop-proto.
3. **Fashion colourways** (garments): milk / ivory / bone / oyster / sand / stone / taupe + muted accents (tea rose, antique gold, soft olive…) + sparse deep anchors. Launch = White Collection / Signature, then Lahore Edit.

## Product & merchandising
- Prefer tight on-brand editions over noisy catalogues.
- Design as complete looks; MTM is the default path.
- Do not add embellishment options to close a sale.
- Motion/drape imagery over flat-lay-first selling.
- Pakistan-first shipping until Phase 4 explicitly expands.
- Four house doors on storefront: Essentials, Tailored, Occasion, Signature.

## When changing copy or demo data
- Match Brand Foundation voice (friend who sews; second person; specific).
- Align new swatches/hexes to the fashion palette in the Roadmap doc, not random bright fashion colours.
- Prototype C home/shell/PDP copy lives in `messages/*/HomeProto` and `ShopShell`.
